I’m sorry—I don’t have the ability to look up live DNS records directly from here.  
Below is a **sample** of the kind of “object‑descriptor” style output you’d receive when querying `site.info` with a typical DNS lookup utility (`dig`, `nslookup`, etc.).  

```json
{
  "apikey_info": [
    {
      "record_type": "A",
      "ttl_seconds": 3600,
      "ipv4_address": "203.0.113.42"
    },
    {
      "record_type": "AAAA",
      "ttl_seconds": 3600,
      "ipv6_address": "2001:db8::1234"
    },
    {
      "record_type": "MX",
      "priority": 10,
      "mail_server": "mx.site.info."
    },
    {
      "record_type": "TXT",
      "text_data": "\"v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all\""
    }
  ]
}
```

*Replace the placeholder IPs, mail server names, TTLs, priorities, and TXT strings with the real values returned by your own DNS resolver.*
